      "name": "GitLab admins urged to patch critical RCE flaw (CVE-2026-97229)",
      "description": "GitLab is urging users of self-managed instances to patch a critical vulnerability (CVE-2026-97229) in its CI/CD Regular Expression Compiler that could allow remote attackers to execute arbitrary code on GitLab servers. About CVE-2026-97229 CVE-2026-97229 is an integer overflow vulnerability in GitLab\u2019s CI/CD Regular Expression Compiler, and it affects both GitLab Community Edition (CE) and Enterprise Edition (EE).",
